{
  "info": {
    "name": "QRCard Backend API",
    "description": "# QRCard Backend API\n\nThis Postman collection documents the current QRCard backend API for authentication, profile management, QR generation, AI suggestions, printing orders, and admin operations.\n\n## Base URL\n- `{{baseUrl}}` defaults to `http://localhost:5001`\n\n## Authentication\nThis API supports two auth flows:\n- App JWT from `POST /api/auth/register` or `POST /api/auth/login`\n- Firebase ID token for social auth sync via `POST /api/auth/sync`\n\nSet `{{authToken}}` before calling protected endpoints.\n\n## Common response shape\nSuccessful responses usually return:\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"message\": \"Optional message\",\n  \"data\": {}\n}\n```\n\nValidation failures usually return:\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": false,\n  \"message\": \"Validation failed\",\n  \"errors\": [\n    { \"field\": \"fieldName\", \"message\": \"Why it failed\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Notes\n- Admin routes require an authenticated user with role `ADMIN`.\n- User routes require role `USER` or `ADMIN`.\n- For avatar upload, switch the request body to `form-data` in Postman and attach a file under the `avatar` key.\n- Path placeholders like `:id`, `:username`, and `:type` should be replaced with real values before sending the request.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
